    "why": "Must show operating cash flow near Goldman's $12.5bn and net debt at target, proving next year's 8.94x multiple too pessimistic."
  },
  "reasons": [
    "The 13 October trading statement pre-announced refining margins of $46.7/bbl and output of 2,190-2,240 mboe/d; Goldman lifted Q3 adjusted net income 18% to $7.49bn, and the $3-4.5bn impairment flagged is non-cash.",
    "BP hit its net debt target ahead of schedule, and interest expense fell 4.4% to $1.18bn in the June quarter \u2014 a saving that survives even if refining margins halve.",
    "Gas & low carbon is guided at 775-795 mboe/d into an LNG [liquefied natural gas] wave the IEA [International Energy Agency] expects to grow demand in 2026 \u2014 the unit taking the write-down still adds volume."
  ],
  "watch": [
    "Operating cash flow: near Goldman's $12.5bn confirms the cash case; well below breaks it, since reported earnings carry the impairment.",
    "Impairments: $3-4.5bn non-cash confirms; anything larger, or cash, breaks the book-entry reading.",
    "Net debt: at or under target confirms deleveraging; an increase breaks the interest-savings reason.",
    "Upstream output: inside 2,190-2,240 mboe/d confirms; a cut to fourth-quarter guidance breaks the volume case."
